title The watch that keeps the loops alive
prompt Keaton: can you detect a session limit and keep the loop alive through the reset, so the hours between the reset and my waking are not missed -- and can incense launch and watch the loops by commanding the tmux pier windows, discovering their names rather than hard-coding 1-8, since that would be a reproduction vulnerability. Jails are off; grant to continue or suggest better.
think The hold seated this morning answers the limit INSIDE a lap. It cannot answer a loop that has already exited, and a loop exits four ways: three instant laps, a spent LOOP_HOURS deadline, an interrupt, a closed terminal. So the ask is right and the answer is a level above the loop.
think tools/l/fleet_watch.sh reads tmux list-windows for window NAMES every pass and matches them against the live seats in construction/fleet-roster.kyri. Keaton named the vulnerability exactly: a layout written into a script stays true until somebody moves a window, and then the watcher types a ship's relaunch into a stranger's keyboard. Seat to tree is the roster's binding, name to index is tmux's, and the watcher adds no third copy of either. A witness asserts zero window indices anywhere in the file.
think The two things a watcher must never do are start a second writer on one checkout and type into a keyboard somebody else holds. The first is read from the process table rather than guessed from a pane's words, because a pane can print anything and a process cannot. The second fails closed: the arm happens only when the pane's last non-blank line ends at a shell prompt.
think And a watcher must not become the thing it prevents. WATCH_ARM_MAX arms that each die inside WATCH_SETTLE stop that seat and report it -- the loop's own quickfail law one level up. It also honors the same wall fleet_rearm.sh prints instead of a paste: .loop-gates-only, .mind-state/CUSTODY, .mind-state/TRANSACTION.
think The arm line drops the git pull the hand-pasted relaunch carries. A hand wants to see a pull refuse; a watcher does not, and an && chain that stops on a dirty tree never reaches the loop. fleet_round_open.sh is the loop's first act and already does strictly more.
obs KEATON'S READ OF THE FLEET WAS AN HOUR STALE AND MINE WOULD HAVE BEEN TOO. He wrote that grass and incense were the only cores running; at 09:01 all six armed loops were mid-lap -- diffuser widening asserts, petrichor repairing a scan that counts its own verdict, pheromone writing control legs, bakery reading stash diffs, grass breaking a repair three ways, copal timing amphora witnesses. A pane read once is a photograph, which is the same reason the watcher reads the process table on every pass rather than trusting what a window last printed.
obs THE JAILS ARE ON, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Keaton wrote that jails are off. ps shows every loop wrapped in ai-jail with --private-home, each mapping its own tree's loops/claude onto ~/.claude, and patchouli's own pane prints Landlock: fully enforced. Named here because it changes what a normal claude login means: the login reached patchouli's jailed credential, which went 281 bytes at 03:19 to 509 at 08:53, and the ship authenticated on its first armed lap.
obs THE WATCH MAKES EXITING STOP MEANING STOP. A loop that prints GATES-ONLY and exits is now brought back on the next pass; the sentinel FILE is what makes a custody stop stick. That consequence is seated in the baton so every ship reads it before it needs it, rather than after.
loom watch=fleet_watch_control pass=14 fail=0 red_sides_proven=2 tmux_session=real
loom fleet=live_loops seats=8 running=7 watcher=1 armed_this_round=patchouli
file tools/l/fleet_watch.sh the watch -- names discovered every pass, five refusals each in the safe direction
file tools/fixtures/l/fleet_watch_control.sh fourteen behaviors on a real tmux session in a pen, every refusal planted and lifted
file tools/f/fleet_watch_witness.rish the guard, rostered tier lap; asserts zero window indices and a roster that is read rather than restated
file tools/l/fleet_baton.txt the WATCH stanza -- the hold, the watch, and the sentinel that makes a stop stick
file .claude/rules/the-baton.md the watch seated as law, with its refusals named
file .cursor/rules/the-baton.mdc the canonical twin, mirrored in the same commit
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri fleet_watch rostered tier lap
scope one watcher built, proven and launched; the fleet at seven running loops and a watch beside them
status GREEN -- fleet_watch, fleet_lap_verdict, fleet_roster, standing_equipment, tracked_link_scan all green on metal
recommend keep-going -- the watch is young and its counters live in memory; the next honest lap is a night's evidence read back out of session-output/watch.txt rather than more mechanism.
